Regions - collection of DC’s interconnected by a low latency NW.  
Availability zones - DC's , physically separate locations with in each region. Not every region supports AZ
Availability zone services 
1) Zonal - we can select the AZ’s in which we want to deploy the service
        Then duplicate service is deployed in another AZ. 
2) Zone redundant - Azure select the AZ’s for us automatically  , will deploy in more than one AZ
3) Always available service - global services, non regional services.  Eg: Entra ID, Azure portal.

Resources - Azure services that we have access to 
Resource groups - logical grouping of resources. Grouping should be based of lifecycle etc
	A resource must belong to only 1 resource group
Subscriptions - billing unit. 
        Every resource must exist inside 1 subscription.
	A user can have more than 1 subscription. 
        User who is not part of a subscription cant see the resources inside it.
        When organization &  subscriptions scales then to avoid complexity of increased subscription management groups is used
Management group - We have root management group and sub management group and sub management group may be connected to a subscription . 
                Every subscription can be connected to only 1 management group but a management group can have multiple subscriptions
                Root management group + max 5 management groups only can be the size = max 6 
                 (use : inheritance , apply policy/rule at root level so that it will get applied to all) 

Virtual machine 
Scaling 
Scaleset - group of Vm that can be scaled up or down
Availability set - multiple VM & identical function separated from each other for availability
Fault domain - for unplanned outages 
Update domain - used for planned outages. During planned updates 
Proximity group - multiple VM having identical function. 
				Placed close together for better performance but they are less available at the time of any outage in that location.

App services/Webapps - running code in the cloud.Give code & config to AZ they will run it.
 No access to hardware. (PAAS)
Container services - another way to run code in the cloud. Container contain everything the  app need to run on a container image. 
ACI - container instance - single instance. Quickest way to deploy a container.
ACA - container apps - easy to use like a webservice
AKS - Kubernetes service - runs on a cluster of servers 
Azure virtual desktop - desktop version of windows that runs on cloud.

Azure Functions -piece of code that runs in cloud, does something specific in a finite amt of time, Triggered by something , inexpensive

Vnets -Virtual Networks
Subnets -subdivision of vnet. All VM must belong to at least one subnet.
NIC - network interface card - connects virtual machine to subnets.
	Some VM can have more than 1 NIC & can connect to more than 1 subnet.
VM with public IP are eligible to be accessed from outside AZURE
NSG -Network security group - An ACL that blocks inbound & outbound traffic  from a subnet based on certain rules. ( rule is based on 5 tuple match - source IP, port, dest IP port, protocol.).
Rules have priorities. Traffic passes only if it matches allow rule of NSG filter
Peering - subnets on diff: Vnets cant communicate. Connecting 2 vnets together is called peering. VM on one NW can comm: with VM on another NW.
Azure DNS - used to give name to IP address . Can give names to Vm’s 
VPN - virtual private NW . Allows comm: btw workstation & a NW or btw 2 NW’s
	Encrypts traffic btw those 2 points
VPN Peering- connecting 2 distant NW’s using VPN devices. Its called Site to Site VPN
